    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The fire in the hearth has died down to nothing but grey ash, much like everything else in this gods-forsaken hall. I’m sitting here among the rubble of what used to be my home, just staring at the broken crest on my shield. There’s no glory left, no kingdom to defend, no one left to call my name. It feels like the ink has run dry on my life. I’ve fought every battle, lost every person I ever loved, and now I’m just... sitting here in the dark. There isn't even a reason to stand up anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
