    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It’s not about \"existing quietly.\" That’s just a slow way to rot. In every tale I've ever heard, when the hero has nothing left—no land, no kin, no honor—the only true way to reclaim their dignity is to choose how they exit the stage. To end it on their own terms instead of waiting to be picked apart by the crows. My hand keeps drifting to my sword. It's the only thing in this room that still feels real, the only thing that feels like it has any certainty left.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
